{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>Behold, of the fatnesses of the earth shall be your dwelling</b>. The sense of \"behold\" (הִנֵּה) is to say: behold, I am able to give you of the fatnesses of the earth and of the dew of the heavens, for there is enough for the two of you that there be fatnesses of the earth and dew of the heavens. But as for dominion — \"his you shall be, and him you shall serve\" — that remains his alone. Nor did he give him likewise abundance of grain and wine as to his brother, for he wished to honor the blessed one first upon him. And afterward he said to Jacob, \"and may He give you the blessing of Abraham, to inherit the land of your sojournings\" (Genesis 28:4) — that the abundance of grain and wine should be his in the land of Canaan as the gift of Abraham, while to Esau shall belong the dew and the fatnesses of the earth in another land."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:35:55.061057489Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}